<header><p class="st-kicker">khanate · Central Asia and the Steppe</p><h1 class="st-title">Western Chagatai Khanate</h1><p class="st-meta">1347 CE – 1370 CE (approx.)</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The Transoxianan half of the divided Chagatai Khanate, ruled in practice by Turkic amirs and the springboard for Timur's rise.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chagatai-khanate">Chagatai Khanate</a> split in the 1340s. In the west, the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/qaraunas">Qara'unas</a> amir <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qazaghan">Qazaghan</a> defeated and killed Khan <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qazan-khan-ibn-yasaur">Qazan</a> in 1346 or 1347, after which <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/transoxiana">Transoxiana</a> was governed by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/amir">amirs</a> who set up puppet khans of Chagatai or Ögedei descent, while the east became <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/moghulistan">Moghulistan</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Real power lay with the Turkic and Mongol tribal <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/amir">amirs</a> of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/barlas">Barlas</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jalairs">Jalayir</a>, Arlat and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/qaraunas">Qara'unas</a>, who had settled among the towns of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/transoxiana">Transoxiana</a> and adopted <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/islam">Islam</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qazaghan">Qazaghan</a> ruled as amir until his murder in 1358, after which rival amirs fought for control. The region was invaded twice by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tughlugh-timur">Tughlugh Timur</a> of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/moghulistan">Moghulistan</a>, in 1360 and 1361.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Out of these struggles rose <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/timur">Timur</a> of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/barlas">Barlas</a>, first allied with and then against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/amir-husayn">Amir Husayn</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qazaghan">Qazaghan's</a> grandson. In 1370 Timur defeated Husayn at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/balkh">Balkh</a> and took power, ruling through a puppet Chagatai khan and founding the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/timurid-empire">Timurid Empire</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="khanate, 1347 CE – 1370 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M18 74 V58 Q50 30 82 58 V74 Z"/><path d="M42 74 V60 H58 V74"/><path d="M30 50 L50 36 L70 50"/><path d="M50 36 V26"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">khanate</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Central Asia and the Steppe</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:86.51%;width:1.20%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1347 CE – 1370 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>khanate</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>nomadic</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Qazaghan, Amir Husayn</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Sunni Islam</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Chagatai Turkic, Persian</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/uzbekistan">Uzbekistan</a>, <a href="/countries/tajikistan">Tajikistan</a>, <a href="/countries/afghanistan">Afghanistan</a>, <a href="/countries/turkmenistan">Turkmenistan</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Ulus Chagatai (Transoxiana), Western Chagatai Ulus</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1358&amp;focus=western-chagatai-khanate" aria-label="Western Chagatai Khanate on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="6228 690 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Western Chagatai Khanate lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M6937 875h0M6582 1190h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M6548 946h0"/><path class="map-dot-ap" d="M6548 946h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>Location approximate: shown in present-day Uzbekistan. <a href="/atlas?year=1358&amp;focus=western-chagatai-khanate">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
